Magnetization studies revealed ferrimagnetic behavior with low magnetic moment. The measured magnetic moments were lower than the values predicted by the Slater-Pauling rule. This reduction is mainly due to structural disorder and tetragonal distortion.

Electrical resistivity measurements showed metallic behavior in both alloys. At low temperature, a small increase in resistivity was observed because of weak localization effects and electron scattering mechanisms.

