The coexistence of cubic and tetragonal phases together with ferrimagnetism makes these materials promising for future spintronic applications.

\section{Conclusion}

This review explains the important findings of CuCoCrAl and CuFeCrAl Heusler alloys. Both materials showed mixed cubic and tetragonal phases along with ferrimagnetic behavior. The alloys also exhibited metallic electrical transport properties. Structural disorder and tetragonal distortion affected their magnetic moments and resistivity behavior. Due to their low magnetic moment and interesting magnetic properties, these alloys may be useful for magnetic memory and spintronic devices.

